          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Pre-symposium and post-symposium workshops will be conducted on October 22 and 23 and on October 26 and 27 respectively. The following workshops are being organised:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Decision-Making in Haemorrhage Control; Pelvic Fracture Management; Early Management of Fractures; Recent Advances in Diagnosis and Management of Abdominal Trauma; Ethical Consideration in Trauma Management; Nursing Management of Trauma Patients; Fundamentals of Tissue Engineering: Hands-on Laboratory Exercises; Obstetric and Sphincter Injury (OASI) and Repair; Child Abuse; and Domestic Violence, Trauma Surveillance, Childhood Injuries and Trauma System ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The University looks forward to this annual event and expects that its outcomes would benefit the wider community. As a part of its social responsibility and commitment to the advancement of health research and education, AKU regularly holds seminars, symposiums and events to raise awareness about health and education related issues which are of national importance and interest."
            }
          ]
        }
